id: design.deadline-propagation
kind: design
title: propagating a deadline across a call
aliases: deadline propagation, context deadline, deadline as a value
tags: design, timeouts, resilience, distributed-systems
questions:
  - how do you pass a deadline to a call you do not control?
  - is a deadline a header, a context value, or a flag?
invariant: A deadline is propagated as a context value or header carrying the absolute instant, not re-derived per hop.
answer_30s: Pass the deadline through (context.WithDeadline in Go, a deadline header in gRPC, or the instant itself); the far side subtracts now in its own clock domain and never assumes the deadline is its own local duration.
when_to_use:
  - any outbound RPC whose caller held its own budget
  - worker queues that must stop work before a hard wall clock
related:
  - design.deadline
  - design.cascading-timeouts
  - design.timeout-budget
sources:
  - https://grpc.io/docs/what-is-grpc/core-improvements/deadlines/
